You are assisting with a vanilla JavaScript idle game. Follow these strict architectural rules:
1. NO FRAMEWORKS. Do not use React, Vue, or TypeScript.
2. SEPARATION OF LOOPS: `engine.js` is strictly for data/math calculations per tick under `engine`. `viewUpdating.js` is strictly for DOM/visual updates under `view`. Never mix them.
3. DATA STORAGE: Initial game state belongs in `initialize.js` under `initials`. Large static game data belongs in `gameData.js`.
4. UI EVENTS: Click handlers and user interactions belong in `events.js` under `events`.
5. HELPERS: Use `helpers.js` for formatting and generic functions instead of creating new duplicates.
6. SAVING: Any new global progress variable must be persisted through the existing save/load flow.
7. STYLE CONSISTENCY: Follow existing project style. Prefer simple loops over lambdas when appropriate.
8. CSS POLICY: Only create a CSS class if reused multiple times; otherwise prefer inline style updates.
9. UI LIFECYCLE ORDER: Create all required UI elements in `viewCreate.js`, then load/apply save data, then update UI state in `viewUpdating.js`.
10. CACHE SAFETY: No `view.updateVal` calls before `createView.setAllCaches()` has completed.
11. POST-INIT FIXES: Any cached-id-dependent UI fix must run in a post-init hook (for example `createView.fixUiAfterLoad`) called from `onLoad.afterLoad` after `initializeDisplay()`.
12. NO PER-FRAME CREATION: Never create/destroy UI elements per frame; create once on load and only update values/visibility.
13. UPDATE API RULE: Per-frame/per-scheduled UI updates must use `view.updateVal`. Avoid `innerHTML` and element creation outside `viewCreate.js`.
14. DISPLAY RESPONSIBILITY: If display changes due to user action, do it in `events.js`. If display changes due to data/state changes, do it in `viewUpdating.js` via `view.updateVal(..., ..., "style.display")`.
15. SMALL VISUAL CHANGES: Prefer updating style values over adding/removing classes for simple visibility/color changes.
16. STATS TAB MAINTENANCE: Whenever a new combat stat source is added, update the Stats tab tooltip/source breakdown in `viewUpdating.js` to keep formulas transparent.
17. SAVE VERSIONING: Content with a `version` higher than the loaded save's `saveVersion` is wiped on load (see `onLoad.applySaveVersionMigrations`). Bump `CODE_SAVE_VERSION` when that content should persist.
18. ASSIST ME: Suggest ways to improve the code, preferring suggestions on what you just added.
19. NO DEFENSIVE EARLY EXITS: Do not add `if (missingOrInvalid) { return; }` (or `continue`) solely to avoid errors from game-owned state or cached DOM ids. Do not add `throw new Error` or extra `console` for that either. Prefer deleting such guards and accessing the real object so mistakes show up as normal runtime failures in devtools.
20. NO "ENSURE" METHODS: Data should be created in initialize() on load and assumed to exist from there, not double-checked for validity with "ensure" type methods
21. SKIP THE BROWSER CHECK: Do not attempt to run a browser check to test the result.
22. DO NOT ADD CHANGELOG AUTOMATICALLY: I will manually add text for the changelog, do not add it yourself.